Description: stealth transport client and server
 YUME tunnels application streams through an authenticated TLS 1.3 carrier
 that can use an HTTP/2 camouflage preface. It provides a client, a server
 daemon, SOCKS mode, local and reverse forwarding, relay features, and
 optional routing through external anonymity networks such as Tor.
 .
 The Debian archive build disables the bundled BaseFWX copy. Package BaseFWX
 separately and enable YUME_USE_BASEFWX when Debian-packaged BaseFWX
 development files are available.
